# Waitlist delivery — src/actions/waitlist.ts
#
# Signups are appended to a Google Sheet by an Apps Script web app. Setup is four
# steps and about five minutes, with NO DNS records to add: tools/waitlist-sheet.gs
# has the instructions. We already run Google Workspace on sudo-cut.com, so the
# list stays inside it and no third party holds it.
#
# Copy to .env.local for development, and set the same two in the Vercel project
# (Settings → Environment Variables) before pointing a domain at this.
#
# WITHOUT THESE THE FORM STILL RENDERS AND STILL VALIDATES, but it cannot store
# anything. It says so to the visitor and offers the support address rather than
# showing a confirmation for a submission that went nowhere. That is deliberate:
# a waitlist that silently drops signups is worse than one that is honestly off.

# The Apps Script deployment's Web app URL. Ends in /exec, not /dev — /dev is the
# test URL and only works while you are signed in, which is a confusing way to
# discover that nothing reaches the sheet in production.
WAITLIST_ENDPOINT=https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycb.../exec

# Must match SECRET in tools/waitlist-sheet.gs. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(crypto.randomUUID())"
WAITLIST_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
